# Oxidean — always on

- Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for stack orientation. Humans: [CONTRIBUTING.md](../../CONTRIBUTING.md), [docs/CODE_PRACTICES.md](../../docs/CODE_PRACTICES.md).
- **Always use in-repo skills** under [`.agents/skills/`](../../.agents/skills/) when they match the task — see [use-in-repo-skills.mdc](use-in-repo-skills.mdc).
- One product: cloud + self-host. Bun workspaces + Cargo crates — do not invent a parallel app structure.
- Web UI is **Octane** (`.tsrx`), not React. Load [`.agents/skills/octane/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/octane/SKILL.md) before UI edits.
- RPC types: change Rust → `make rpc-gen`. Never treat hand-edited `packages/api-client` as source of truth.
- DB dialects only inside `crates/oxidean-db`.
- No secrets in commits or examples. Prefer `make test` / `make rpc-sync-check` / relevant e2e before claiming done.
- **Before committing `apps/web` changes:** run `make web-lint` and `make web-format-check` (`@tsrx/oxc` — type-aware oxlint + oxfmt). Fix failures; do not skip. Plain `tsc` is not the web type gate yet (see [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)).
- Scratch/temp files go under gitignored [`tmp/`](../../tmp/README.md) (never the repo root).
- Prefer extending existing patterns (Query session helpers, auth gates, Make targets) over new frameworks.
- No AI co-author / tooling attribution on commits or PRs — see [no-ai-attribution.mdc](no-ai-attribution.mdc).
